---
// Post-purchase delivery page for the Advanced Ribbon Modules (2026-07-23).
//
// RETIRED 2026-09-03. The delivery keys are deleted from R2 and the pack is no longer
// sold standalone: from 2.0 the ribbon modules are part of the subscription (EULA
// section 6). The standalone buy link went null at the switch, so nothing redirects here
// any more and the page has no audience.
//
// KEPT RATHER THAN DELETED for one reason: a pre-switch Stripe receipt could still send
// somebody here, and a page that explains where the modules went is worth more than a
// 404. Adrian confirmed nobody bought the pack ("nobody paid for the ribbons anyway"),
// which is why the R2 objects could go at all - a $199 perpetual licence with a purchaser
// behind it could not have been stranded.
//
// Do NOT re-add a download button. There is no object to point it at, and the modules
// arrive with a subscription now.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import NavBar from '../../components/NavBar.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import BracketButton from '../../components/BracketButton.astro';

---
<BaseLayout
  title="Thank you | FabricatorStudio"
  description="Your Advanced Ribbon Modules download."
  noindex
>
  <NavBar />

  <section id="thanks">
    <p class="ty-eyebrow">ADVANCED RIBBON MODULES</p>
    <h1 class="ty-head">Thank you. They're yours.</h1>
    <p class="ty-sub">If you bought the pack before FabricatorStudio 2.0, it stays yours on the terms you bought it under. Your receipt arrives by email from Stripe.</p>

    <div class="ty-card">
      <BracketButton kind="hard" href="/account/" label="Go to your account" event="thankyou-account" />
      <p class="ty-keep">The ribbon modules are part of the Studio Pipeline subscription now, and arrive with it. They are no longer a separate download. If you bought the standalone pack and need it, email <a href="mailto:contact@fabricator.studio">contact@fabricator.studio</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ty-steps">
      <h2 class="ty-steps__head">Where the modules are now</h2>
      <p class="ty-note">Ribbon Spine, Arm and Leg ship inside the Studio Pipeline from 2.0 and appear in the Build Modules picker with no separate install. Every tier from Freelance Tech Art + Animation up carries them. Anything misbehaving? <a href="mailto:contact@fabricator.studio">contact@fabricator.studio</a> is the fastest way to reach me.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  #thanks { text-align: left; max-width: 46rem; }
  .ty-eyebrow { margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.8125rem; letter-spacing: 0.18em; color: var(--bone); }
  .ty-head { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 400; font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 2.75rem); line-height: 1.05; color: var(--bone); }
  .ty-sub { margin: 0 0 1.75rem; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--bone-dim); text-wrap: pretty; }
  .ty-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    padding: 1.75rem;
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: linear-gradient(120deg, rgba(124, 255, 178, 0.1), rgba(124, 255, 178, 0)), var(--carbon);
    border: 1px solid rgba(124, 255, 178, 0.22);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--plasma);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
  }
  .ty-keep { margin: 0; font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--bone-faint); }
  .ty-steps { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .ty-steps__head { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.0625rem; color: var(--bone); }
  .ty-steps__list { margin: 0 0 1rem; padding-left: 1.25rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; color: var(--bone-dim); font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .ty-steps__list code { color: var(--bone); }
  .ty-steps__list b { color: var(--bone); }
  .ty-note { margin: 0; font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--bone-faint); }
</style>
